@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nii-il05-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il05-published-figures`

-- National Insurance Law [Consolidated Version], Schedule K (לוח י״א) — maximum and minimum income for
-- insurance contributions. Quotations (`src:N`) are copied mechanically from line N of
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/national-insurance-law-consolidated-version-5755-1995.he.wiki.txt.
--
-- WHAT IT IS. A table of four items (employee; self-employed; the insured of s 348(d) and (e);
-- another insured), each with a maximum and a minimum income, per month (item 1 only), per quarter and
-- per year. s 348(a) disregards income above the maximum, s 348(b) raises income below the minimum.
-- The schedule is written in terms of three figures it does not print (the basic amount, the average
-- wage, the minimum wage); the rules below take them from a `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax
-- year` record and, for item 1's minimum, from the employee's own minimum wage.
--
-- WHICH YEARS (NOTES.md, assumption A1). Contribution periods from January 2026. Schedule K's own text
-- carries no tag later than 5772 (2012), so it was probably the same in 2025, but this row answers
-- from 2026 only, with row IL-04, whose s 334 and Schedule J are the text from 1 January 2026, and
-- because s 342 is (NOTES.md section 1). For 2026 the published figures are used; for a later year a
-- caller who has the figures uses the rules that take them as an argument.

§ `Schedule K — maximum and minimum income for insurance contributions`
-- src:4751 | לוח י״א
-- src:4752 | [note: (סעיפים 345(ה), 348, ו־349)]
-- src:4753 | הכנסה מרבית ומזערית לענין דמי ביטוח [תיקון: תשס״ב־7, תשס״ג־12]
-- src:4755 | [תיקון: תשנ״ט, ק״ת תשנ״ט, תש״ס־2, תשס״ב־7, תשס״ג־12, תשס״ד־6, תשס״ט־4, תשע״א־3, תשע״ב־2]

@ref National Insurance Law ss 342 and 348 and Schedule K; this row's scope (NOTES.md assumption A1)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`this row answers contribution periods from January 2026 only` MEANS
    REFUSE "this row answers contribution periods from January 2026 only"

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K, "רבעון" (source line 4771)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12` MEANS
    REFUSE "a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12"

§§ `"quarter"`

-- src:4769 | [תיקון: תשנ״ט]
-- src:4770 | בלוח זה,
-- src:4771 | ”רבעון“ – תקופה של שלושה חודשים רצופים המתחילה ב־1 בינואר, ב־1 באפריל, ב־1 ביולי או ב־1 באוקטובר של כל שנת מס;
-- "a period of three consecutive months beginning on 1 January, 1 April, 1 July or 1 October of each
-- tax year". A tax year is a calendar year (nii-il05-nouns.l4).
@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K, "רבעון" (source line 4771)
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A quarter of a tax year`
`the quarter that contains month` `the month` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the month` LESS THAN 1  THEN `a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12`
           IF `the month` AT MOST   3  THEN `the quarter beginning on 1 January`
           IF `the month` AT MOST   6  THEN `the quarter beginning on 1 April`
           IF `the month` AT MOST   9  THEN `the quarter beginning on 1 July`
           IF `the month` AT MOST   12 THEN `the quarter beginning on 1 October`
           OTHERWISE                       `a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12`

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K, "רבעון" (source line 4771)
GIVEN q IS A `A quarter of a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first month of` q MEANS
    CONSIDER q
    WHEN `the quarter beginning on 1 January` THEN 1
    WHEN `the quarter beginning on 1 April`   THEN 4
    WHEN `the quarter beginning on 1 July`    THEN 7
    WHEN `the quarter beginning on 1 October` THEN 10

-- The quarters "of that tax year", over which each item's yearly figure is summed.
@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K, "רבעון" (source line 4771)
GIVETH A LIST OF `A quarter of a tax year`
`the four quarters of a tax year` MEANS
    LIST `the quarter beginning on 1 January`, `the quarter beginning on 1 April`
       , `the quarter beginning on 1 July`, `the quarter beginning on 1 October`

§§ `"basic amount" and "the average wage" of a month`

-- src:4773 | ”הסכום הבסיסי“ – כהגדרתו בפסקה (3) שבהגדרה [note: ”ה]סכום [note: ה]בסיסי[note: “] שבסעיף 1.
-- "as defined in paragraph (3) of the definition 'basic amount' in section 1": the figure in the record.
@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K, "הסכום הבסיסי" (source line 4773); s 1 "הסכום הבסיסי" (3) (source line 191)
GIVEN f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the basic amount, under` f MEANS
    f's `the basic amount under paragraph (3) of its definition in section 1`

-- The average wage "of" a month is the one in force in it: the figure as updated on 1 January, or on
-- the latest later update day not after that month (s 1 "יום העדכון", source line 225). Updates are
-- listed in order of month (input convention), so a later qualifying one replaces an earlier one.
GIVEN `the month`   IS A NUMBER
      `the figure`  IS A NUMBER
      `the updates` IS A LIST OF `An update of the average wage within the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the average wage in force in month` `the month` `, starting from` `the figure` `, after the updates` `the updates` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the updates`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `the figure`
    WHEN u FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF   u's `the month of the update` AT MOST `the month`
        THEN `the average wage in force in month` `the month` `, starting from` (u's `the average wage as updated`) `, after the updates` rest
        ELSE `the average wage in force in month` `the month` `, starting from` `the figure` `, after the updates` rest

@ref National Insurance Law s 1 "השכר הממוצע" and "יום העדכון" (source lines 222-225), as Schedule K reads it (source lines 4761-4765)
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER
      f           IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the average wage of month` `the month` `, under` f MEANS
    `the average wage in force in month` `the month` `, starting from` (f's `the average wage as updated on 1 January`) `, after the updates` (f's `later updates of the average wage in the tax year`)

§§ `"minimum wage" of the first month of a quarter`

-- src:4772 | ”שכר מינימום“ – שכר מינימום, שכר מינימום חלקי, שכר מינימום יומי, או שכר מינימום לשעה החל, לפי הענין, לפי הוראות חוק שכר מינימום לגבי עובד פלוני;
@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K, "שכר מינימום" (source line 4772)
GIVEN q IS A `A quarter of a tax year`
      w IS A `The minimum wage applicable to the employee in the first month of each quarter`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum wage applicable to the employee in the first month of` q `, under` w MEANS
    CONSIDER q
    WHEN `the quarter beginning on 1 January` THEN w's `in January`
    WHEN `the quarter beginning on 1 April`   THEN w's `in April`
    WHEN `the quarter beginning on 1 July`    THEN w's `in July`
    WHEN `the quarter beginning on 1 October` THEN w's `in October`

§§ `Item 1 — an employee`

-- src:4757 | פרט | בעד | הכנסה מרבית | הכנסה מזערית |
-- src:4758 | 1. | עובד | לחודש – הסכום הבסיסי, כפול 5; | לחודש – סכום השווה לשכר מינימום של החודש הראשון ברבעון; |
-- src:4759 | לרבעון – סכום השווה להכנסה המרבית לחודש, כפול 3; | לרבעון – סכום השווה להכנסה המזערית לחודש, כפול 3; |
-- src:4760 | לשנה – סכום השווה לסך ההכנסות המרביות בכל רבעון שבאותה שנת מס. | לשנה – סכום השווה לסך ההכנסות המזעריות שבכל רבעון שבאותה שנת מס. |
-- Maximum: "for a month – the basic amount, times 5; for a quarter – a sum equal to the maximum income
-- for a month, times 3; for a year – a sum equal to the total of the maximum incomes in each quarter
-- of that tax year." Minimum: "for a month – a sum equal to the minimum wage of the first month of the
-- quarter; for a quarter – a sum equal to the minimum income for a month, times 3; for a year – a sum
-- equal to the total of the minimum incomes in each quarter of that tax year."
@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K item 1, maximum, for a month (source line 4758)
GIVEN f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K item 1 — the maximum income for a month, under` f MEANS
    `the basic amount, under` f TIMES 5

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K item 1, maximum, for a quarter (source line 4759)
GIVEN f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K item 1 — the maximum income for a quarter, under` f MEANS
    `Schedule K item 1 — the maximum income for a month, under` f TIMES 3

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K item 1, maximum, for a year (source line 4760)
GIVEN f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K item 1 — the maximum income for a year, under` f MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN q YIELD `Schedule K item 1 — the maximum income for a quarter, under` f) `the four quarters of a tax year`)

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K item 1, minimum, for a month (source line 4758)
GIVEN q IS A `A quarter of a tax year`
      w IS A `The minimum wage applicable to the employee in the first month of each quarter`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K item 1 — the minimum income for a month in` q `, under` w MEANS
    `the minimum wage applicable to the employee in the first month of` q `, under` w

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K item 1, minimum, for a quarter (source line 4759)
GIVEN q IS A `A quarter of a tax year`
      w IS A `The minimum wage applicable to the employee in the first month of each quarter`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K item 1 — the minimum income for` q `, under` w MEANS
    `Schedule K item 1 — the minimum income for a month in` q `, under` w TIMES 3

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K item 1, minimum, for a year (source line 4760)
GIVEN w IS A `The minimum wage applicable to the employee in the first month of each quarter`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K item 1 — the minimum income for a year, under` w MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN q YIELD `Schedule K item 1 — the minimum income for` q `, under` w) `the four quarters of a tax year`)

§§ `Item 2 — a self-employed person`

-- src:4761 | 2. | עובד עצמאי | לרבעון – סכום השווה לחמש פעמים הסכום הבסיסי, כפול 3; | לרבעון – סכום השווה ל־25% מהשכר הממוצע של החודש הראשון ברבעון, כפול 3; |
-- src:4762 | לשנה – סכום השווה לסך ההכנסות המרביות לכל רבעון שבאותה שנת מס. | לשנה – סכום השווה לסך ההכנסות המזעריות בכל רבעון שבאותה שנת מס. |
-- Maximum: "for a quarter – a sum equal to five times the basic amount, times 3; for a year – the total
-- of the maximum incomes for each quarter of that tax year." Minimum: "for a quarter – a sum equal to
-- 25% of the average wage of the first month of the quarter, times 3; for a year – the total of the
-- minimum incomes in each quarter of that tax year." No figure for a month (fork F2).
@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K item 2, maximum, for a quarter (source line 4761)
GIVEN f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K item 2 — the maximum income for a quarter, under` f MEANS
    5 TIMES `the basic amount, under` f TIMES 3

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K item 2, maximum, for a year (source line 4762)
GIVEN f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K item 2 — the maximum income for a year, under` f MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN q YIELD `Schedule K item 2 — the maximum income for a quarter, under` f) `the four quarters of a tax year`)

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K item 2, minimum, for a quarter (source line 4761)
GIVEN q IS A `A quarter of a tax year`
      f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K item 2 — the minimum income for` q `, under` f MEANS
    25% TIMES `the average wage of month` (`the first month of` q) `, under` f TIMES 3

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K item 2, minimum, for a year (source line 4762)
GIVEN f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K item 2 — the minimum income for a year, under` f MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN q YIELD `Schedule K item 2 — the minimum income for` q `, under` f) `the four quarters of a tax year`)

§§ `Items 3 and 4 — the average wage they read`

-- Items 3 and 4 do not read the average wage of each quarter's first month, as item 2 does: "for the
-- quarters beginning on 1 January, 1 April and 1 July of a tax year – … of the average wage of the
-- first month in the quarter beginning on 1 January, times 3, and for the quarter beginning on
-- 1 October of a tax year – … of the average wage of the first month of that quarter, times 3".
@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K items 3 and 4, minimum, for a quarter (source lines 4763, 4765)
GIVEN q IS A `A quarter of a tax year`
      f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the average wage items 3 and 4 read for` q `, under` f MEANS
    CONSIDER q
    WHEN `the quarter beginning on 1 October` THEN `the average wage of month` 10 `, under` f
    OTHERWISE                                     `the average wage of month` 1  `, under` f

§§ `Item 3 — an insured person as stated in section 348(d) and (e)`

-- src:4763 | 3. | מבוטח כאמור בסעיף 348(ד) ו־(ה) | לרבעון או לשנה – סכום השווה להכנסה המרבית לרבעון או לשנה, כאמור בפרט 1, לפי הענין. | לרבעון שתחילתו ב־1 בינואר, ב־1 באפריל וב־1 ביולי של שנת מס – סכום השווה ל־5% מהשכר הממוצע של החודש הראשון ברבעון שתחילתו ב־1 בינואר, כפול 3, ולרבעון שתחילתו ב־1 באוקטובר של שנת מס – סכום השווה ל־5% מהשכר הממוצע של החודש הראשון שבאותו רבעון, כפול 3; |
-- src:4764 | לשנה – סכום השווה לסך ההכנסות המזעריות שבכל רבעון שבאותה שנת מס. |
-- Maximum: "for a quarter or a year – a sum equal to the maximum income for a quarter or a year, as
-- stated in item 1, as the case may be." Minimum: 5% of the average wage item 3 reads (above), times
-- 3, for a quarter; for a year, the total over the quarters.
@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K item 3, maximum (source line 4763)
GIVEN f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K item 3 — the maximum income for a quarter, under` f MEANS
    `Schedule K item 1 — the maximum income for a quarter, under` f

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K item 3, maximum (source line 4763)
GIVEN f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K item 3 — the maximum income for a year, under` f MEANS
    `Schedule K item 1 — the maximum income for a year, under` f

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K item 3, minimum, for a quarter (source line 4763)
GIVEN q IS A `A quarter of a tax year`
      f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K item 3 — the minimum income for` q `, under` f MEANS
    5% TIMES `the average wage items 3 and 4 read for` q `, under` f TIMES 3

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K item 3, minimum, for a year (source line 4764)
GIVEN f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K item 3 — the minimum income for a year, under` f MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN q YIELD `Schedule K item 3 — the minimum income for` q `, under` f) `the four quarters of a tax year`)

§§ `Item 4 — another insured person`

-- src:4765 | 4. | מבוטח אחר | לרבעון או לשנה – סכום השווה להכנסה המרבית לרבעון או לשנה, כאמור בפרט 2, לפי הענין. | לרבעון שתחילתו ב־1 בינואר, ב־1 באפריל וב־1 ביולי של שנת מס – סכום השווה ל־15% מהשכר הממוצע של החודש הראשון ברבעון שתחילתו ב־1 בינואר, כפול 3, ולרבעון שתחילתו ב־1 באוקטובר של שנת מס – סכום השווה ל־15% מהשכר הממוצע של החודש הראשון שבאותו רבעון, כפול 3; |
-- src:4766 | לשנה – סכום השווה לסך ההכנסות המזעריות שבכל רבעון שבאותה שנת מס. |
-- Maximum: as stated in item 2. Minimum: 15% of the average wage item 4 reads, times 3, for a quarter;
-- for a year, the total over the quarters.
@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K item 4, maximum (source line 4765)
GIVEN f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K item 4 — the maximum income for a quarter, under` f MEANS
    `Schedule K item 2 — the maximum income for a quarter, under` f

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K item 4, maximum (source line 4765)
GIVEN f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K item 4 — the maximum income for a year, under` f MEANS
    `Schedule K item 2 — the maximum income for a year, under` f

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K item 4, minimum, for a quarter (source line 4765)
GIVEN q IS A `A quarter of a tax year`
      f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K item 4 — the minimum income for` q `, under` f MEANS
    15% TIMES `the average wage items 3 and 4 read for` q `, under` f TIMES 3

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K item 4, minimum, for a year (source line 4766)
GIVEN f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K item 4 — the minimum income for a year, under` f MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN q YIELD `Schedule K item 4 — the minimum income for` q `, under` f) `the four quarters of a tax year`)

§§ `A month, for items 2, 3 and 4`

-- Items 2-4 print no monthly figure, but s 337(a)(2) charges the self-employed and others on annual
-- income divided into advance periods, which are months unless the Minister sets otherwise (s 336),
-- and s 348(d) speaks of a month. Every quarterly figure in the schedule is written as a monthly
-- amount "times 3", so a month's figure is taken as a third of its quarter's (NOTES.md, fork F2).
-- The Institute prints monthly figures exactly so: 51,910 a month for a self-employed person (5 times
-- 10,382) and 3,442 (25% of 13,769) for the minimum (tests module).
@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K items 2-4 (source lines 4761-4766); NOTES.md fork F2
GIVEN `the figure for the quarter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`a month's share of the quarter's figure` `the figure for the quarter` MEANS
    `the figure for the quarter` DIVIDED BY 3

§§ `The maximum and the minimum, by item and period`

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K, maximum income (source lines 4758-4766)
GIVEN `the item` IS AN `An item of Schedule K`
      `the period` IS A `A period under Schedule K`
      f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum income under Schedule K for` `the item` `, for` `the period` `, under` f MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period`
    WHEN `the whole tax year` THEN
        CONSIDER `the item`
        WHEN `item 1, an employee`                                            THEN `Schedule K item 1 — the maximum income for a year, under` f
        WHEN `item 2, a self-employed person`                                 THEN `Schedule K item 2 — the maximum income for a year, under` f
        WHEN `item 3, an insured person as stated in section 348(d) and (e)` THEN `Schedule K item 3 — the maximum income for a year, under` f
        WHEN `item 4, another insured person`                                 THEN `Schedule K item 4 — the maximum income for a year, under` f
    WHEN `a quarter of the tax year` q THEN `the quarter's maximum`
    WHEN `a month of the tax year` m THEN
        CONSIDER `the item`
        WHEN `item 1, an employee` THEN `Schedule K item 1 — the maximum income for a month, under` f
        OTHERWISE                       `a month's share of the quarter's figure` `the quarter's maximum`
    WHERE
        `the quarter's maximum` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the item`
            WHEN `item 1, an employee`                                            THEN `Schedule K item 1 — the maximum income for a quarter, under` f
            WHEN `item 2, a self-employed person`                                 THEN `Schedule K item 2 — the maximum income for a quarter, under` f
            WHEN `item 3, an insured person as stated in section 348(d) and (e)` THEN `Schedule K item 3 — the maximum income for a quarter, under` f
            WHEN `item 4, another insured person`                                 THEN `Schedule K item 4 — the maximum income for a quarter, under` f

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K item 1: the minimum wage applicable to a particular employee (source line 4772)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Schedule K item 1's minimum is the minimum wage applicable to the particular employee, which the case does not give` MEANS
    REFUSE "Schedule K item 1's minimum is the minimum wage applicable to the particular employee, which the case does not give"

-- `w`: the employee's minimum wage, for item 1; NOTHING for anyone else.
@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K, minimum income (source lines 4758-4766)
GIVEN `the item`   IS AN `An item of Schedule K`
      `the period` IS A `A period under Schedule K`
      f            IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
      w            IS A MAYBE `The minimum wage applicable to the employee in the first month of each quarter`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum income under Schedule K for` `the item` `, for` `the period` `, under` f `and` w MEANS
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `item 1, an employee` THEN
        CONSIDER w
        WHEN NOTHING     THEN `Schedule K item 1's minimum is the minimum wage applicable to the particular employee, which the case does not give`
        WHEN JUST `the employee's minimum wage` THEN
            CONSIDER `the period`
            WHEN `the whole tax year`          THEN `Schedule K item 1 — the minimum income for a year, under` `the employee's minimum wage`
            WHEN `a quarter of the tax year` q THEN `Schedule K item 1 — the minimum income for` q `, under` `the employee's minimum wage`
            WHEN `a month of the tax year` m   THEN `Schedule K item 1 — the minimum income for a month in` (`the quarter that contains month` m) `, under` `the employee's minimum wage`
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the period`
        WHEN `the whole tax year`          THEN `the year's minimum`
        WHEN `a quarter of the tax year` q THEN `the quarter's minimum` q
        WHEN `a month of the tax year` m   THEN `a month's share of the quarter's figure` (`the quarter's minimum` (`the quarter that contains month` m))
    WHERE
        `the year's minimum` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the item`
            WHEN `item 2, a self-employed person`                                 THEN `Schedule K item 2 — the minimum income for a year, under` f
            WHEN `item 3, an insured person as stated in section 348(d) and (e)` THEN `Schedule K item 3 — the minimum income for a year, under` f
            OTHERWISE                                                                  `Schedule K item 4 — the minimum income for a year, under` f
        `the quarter's minimum` q MEANS
            CONSIDER `the item`
            WHEN `item 2, a self-employed person`                                 THEN `Schedule K item 2 — the minimum income for` q `, under` f
            WHEN `item 3, an insured person as stated in section 348(d) and (e)` THEN `Schedule K item 3 — the minimum income for` q `, under` f
            OTHERWISE                                                                  `Schedule K item 4 — the minimum income for` q `, under` f

§§ `The figures for a tax year`

-- For 2026, the Institute's published figures (nii-il05-published-figures.l4), with the average wage
-- as calculated under s 2 (fork F1) and no update after 1 January (the Institute's page lists none).
@ref National Insurance Institute figures for 2026 (nii-il05-published-figures.l4); NOTES.md fork F1
GIVETH A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
`the figures Schedule K reads for 2026, as published` MEANS
    `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year` WITH
        `tax year`                                                            IS 2026
        `the basic amount under paragraph (3) of its definition in section 1` IS `the basic amount under paragraph (3) from 1 January 2026, as published by the National Insurance Institute`
        `the average wage as updated on 1 January`                            IS `the average wage from 1 January 2026 as calculated under section 2, for contributions, as published by the National Insurance Institute`
        `later updates of the average wage in the tax year`                   IS EMPTY

@ref National Insurance Law s 1 "הסכום הבסיסי" and "השכר הממוצע": the figures from 1 January 2027 were not published on 2026-10-06
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the figures Schedule K reads for 2027 and later had not been published when this encoding was made` MEANS
    REFUSE "the figures Schedule K reads for 2027 and later had not been published when this encoding was made"

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K (source lines 4751-4773); NOTES.md assumption A1
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
`the figures Schedule K reads for the tax year` `the year` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the year` AT LEAST 2027 THEN `the figures Schedule K reads for 2027 and later had not been published when this encoding was made`
           IF `the year` EQUALS   2026 THEN `the figures Schedule K reads for 2026, as published`
           OTHERWISE                        `this row answers contribution periods from January 2026 only`

-- The full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over, for the first months of the quarters
-- of 2026, as the Institute publishes it. It is Schedule K's "minimum wage" only for an employee to
-- whom the full monthly minimum wage applies (fork F11).
@ref National Insurance Institute, "minimum wage", fetched 2026-10-06 (nii-il05-published-figures.l4)
GIVETH A `The minimum wage applicable to the employee in the first month of each quarter`
`the full monthly minimum wage in the first month of each quarter of 2026` MEANS
    `The minimum wage applicable to the employee in the first month of each quarter` WITH
        `in January` IS `the monthly minimum wage for an employee aged 18 or over from 1 April 2025, as published by the National Insurance Institute`
        `in April`   IS `the monthly minimum wage for an employee aged 18 or over from 1 April 2026, as published by the National Insurance Institute`
        `in July`    IS `the monthly minimum wage for an employee aged 18 or over from 1 April 2026, as published by the National Insurance Institute`
        `in October` IS `the monthly minimum wage for an employee aged 18 or over from 1 April 2026, as published by the National Insurance Institute`
